Package: regsimsize
Type: Package
Title: Simulation-Based Power and Sample Size for Regression Models
Version: 0.1.1
Authors@R: person(given = c("Yasser", "C"), family = "Bouklouch",
    role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "Yasser.bouklouch@gmail.com")
Description: Estimate rejection probabilities and select sample sizes by
    repeatedly generating study data, fitting the planned analysis, and
    testing a prespecified hypothesis. Provides constructors for generalized
    linear, linear, and proportional hazards models, and function interfaces
    for other data generators, model fitters, and tests. Reports Monte Carlo
    uncertainty, failed analyses, and event summaries. Simulation reporting
    follows principles discussed by Morris, White, and Crowther (2019)
    <doi:10.1002/sim.8086>.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
URL: https://github.com/BCYasser/regsimsize
BugReports: https://github.com/BCYasser/regsimsize/issues
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports: stats, graphics, grDevices, utils, parallel, survival
Suggests: nlme, knitr
VignetteBuilder: knitr
NeedsCompilation: no
